### 1. POST gültig -> 200/201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/trainings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-09-06",
  "distanceKm": 10,
  "durationMinutes": 48,
  "averageHeartRate": 151
}


### 2. POST versucht id und pace zu setzen -> Backend soll sie ignorieren
POST http://localhost:8080/api/trainings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 999,
  "pace": 2.5,
  "date": "2026-09-06",
  "distanceKm": 10,
  "durationMinutes": 50,
  "averageHeartRate": 145
}


### 3. PUT gültig -> bestehendes Training ändern
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/trainings/5
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-09-07",
  "distanceKm": 12,
  "durationMinutes": 60,
  "averageHeartRate": 148
}


### 4. PUT ungültige Distanz -> 400
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/trainings/5
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-09-07",
  "distanceKm": -12,
  "durationMinutes": 60,
  "averageHeartRate": 148
}


### 5. PUT ungültige Herzfrequenz -> 400
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/trainings/5
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-09-07",
  "distanceKm": 12,
  "durationMinutes": 60,
  "averageHeartRate": 300
}


### 6. PUT nicht vorhandene ID -> 404
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/trainings/99999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-09-07",
  "distanceKm": 12,
  "durationMinutes": 60,
  "averageHeartRate": 148
}


### 7. GET kontrollieren
GET http://localhost:8080/api/trainings/5
